Verdict: NEED_MORE
Rationale: The claim has three material parts: (1) the 2004 World Series of Poker gold bracelet holder, (2) their role as the 2011 Commissioner, and (3) Michael McDonald being the youngest person to win an event in 2011. The first part is not established as the 2004 bracelet holder is not identified in the evidence. The second part is partially supported by evidence that Jeffrey Pollack held a Commissioner-like role in 2011, but it is not explicitly stated that he was the 2011 World Series of Poker Commissioner. The third part is contradicted by evidence showing Annette Obrestad was the youngest winner in 2007. Further evidence is needed to confirm the 2004 bracelet holder and the 2011 Commissioner role.
